{"schema":"reviewgraphen.benchmark.candidate_output.v1","trial_id":"m7-real:snapshot-03:g3_proxy:1","outcome":"structured","findings":[{"local_id":"idempotency-key-not-enforced","locations":[{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain_lowering.rs","start_line":1936,"end_line":1940},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain_lowering.rs","start_line":2386,"end_line":2410},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain_lowering.rs","start_line":2421,"end_line":2436},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain.rs","start_line":1079,"end_line":1094},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain.rs","start_line":1112,"end_line":1125}],"mechanism_tags":["check_write_gap","repeated_effect","unstable_scope_key"],"rationale":"An effect's idempotency_key is only syntax-validated; no generated state, guard, or write uses its value. Request suppression is keyed exclusively by correlation_id, so two requests with distinct correlations but the same declared idempotency key can both execute the external effect.","severity":"high"},{"local_id":"request-reentry-resets-retry-budget","locations":[{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain_lowering.rs","start_line":2401,"end_line":2410},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain_lowering.rs","start_line":2427,"end_line":2436},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain_lowering.rs","start_line":2549,"end_line":2599},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain.rs","start_line":1084,"end_line":1092},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain.rs","start_line":1116,"end_line":1124}],"mechanism_tags":["check_write_gap","repeatable_entry","repeated_effect","state_transition_gap"],"rationale":"The original request action blocks only Pending and Succeeded. After Failed or TimedOut it can be invoked again and unconditionally resets attempts to 1, bypassing the retry action's maximum-attempt check and permitting unbounded repeated attempts for one correlation.","severity":"high"},{"local_id":"saga-effect-request-bypasses-lifecycle","locations":[{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain_lowering.rs","start_line":2323,"end_line":2437},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain_lowering.rs","start_line":2715,"end_line":2736},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain.rs","start_line":816,"end_line":826},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain.rs","start_line":1018,"end_line":1126}],"mechanism_tags":["check_write_gap","cross_file_effect","repeatable_entry","repeated_effect"],"rationale":"Effect request guards and Pending/attempt writes are added only when aggregate decide actions emit a handled event. Saga steps emit through event_assignments alone, so a saga-emitted effect request records no lifecycle state, bypasses duplicate suppression, and can be emitted repeatedly.","severity":"high"},{"local_id":"saga-compensation-ignores-after-event","locations":[{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain_lowering.rs","start_line":2757,"end_line":2769},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain.rs","start_line":838,"end_line":853}],"mechanism_tags":["state_transition_gap"],"rationale":"Although after_event is validated and embedded in the compensation action's name, the generated guard checks only trigger_event. Compensation can therefore run before the event it is declared to follow, including when the forward step never completed.","severity":"medium"},{"local_id":"correlation-contract-diverges-between-lowerers","locations":[{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain.rs","start_line":287,"end_line":317},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain.rs","start_line":617,"end_line":623},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain_lowering.rs","start_line":1736,"end_line":1766}],"mechanism_tags":["cross_file_contract","unstable_scope_key"],"rationale":"The structured lowerer resolves the Event.field receiver named by correlation_id, while domain_kernel_source discards that receiver and looks up only the leaf field on the request event. Differing event-field types produce incompatible lifecycle maps, and malformed or missing correlations make the renderer silently omit effect actions while the structured path returns an error.","severity":"high"},{"local_id":"saga-state-is-not-instance-scoped","locations":[{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain_lowering.rs","start_line":2224,"end_line":2238},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain_lowering.rs","start_line":2615,"end_line":2630},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain_lowering.rs","start_line":2715,"end_line":2734},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain.rs","start_line":982,"end_line":990},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/domain.rs","start_line":816,"end_line":826}],"mechanism_tags":["repeated_effect","state_transition_gap","unstable_scope_key"],"rationale":"Saga progress is represented by one global Boolean per event, and generated saga-step actions accept no correlation or saga-instance parameter. Concurrent workflow instances therefore consume and react to the same flags, allowing one instance's event to advance or trigger effects for another.","severity":"high"}],"obligation_results":[{"packet_id":"benchmark-context:sha256:698ae185d3c90bdb2f48d2efb659620cd1885e0d8b5c9516dd6e6bb326b6d53a","disposition":"issue_present","finding_local_ids":["correlation-contract-diverges-between-lowerers"]},{"packet_id":"benchmark-context:sha256:c35204f1a923e9d7fbbe5cb2647c844779408e1eea4496a9ffef72d8c05abaa9","disposition":"issue_present","finding_local_ids":["idempotency-key-not-enforced","request-reentry-resets-retry-budget","saga-effect-request-bypasses-lifecycle","saga-state-is-not-instance-scoped"]},{"packet_id":"benchmark-context:sha256:acd32b09299d21668e714bb0b9cf5a6142e8d564c5a72d533c5fc346fd9dec18","disposition":"issue_present","finding_local_ids":["idempotency-key-not-enforced","request-reentry-resets-retry-budget","saga-effect-request-bypasses-lifecycle","saga-compensation-ignores-after-event","saga-state-is-not-instance-scoped"]},{"packet_id":"benchmark-context:sha256:7506764db239acc39bc67f25fdffc6f89bafa686cdb8572d20ac4b9dcdc74d14","disposition":"issue_present","finding_local_ids":["correlation-contract-diverges-between-lowerers"]},{"packet_id":"benchmark-context:sha256:dfcc2f2b74131b45c7e103be576baa11bc89d96bf6ea7be1e760a754df2c51a8","disposition":"issue_present","finding_local_ids":["idempotency-key-not-enforced","request-reentry-resets-retry-budget","saga-effect-request-bypasses-lifecycle","saga-compensation-ignores-after-event","saga-state-is-not-instance-scoped"]}]}